.PP
\f[B]observe\f[R] tokenizes \f[I]line\f[R], looks up or creates the
per\-system profile, updates statistics, and returns
\f[B]Some(Anomaly)\f[R] if the event is anomalous.
Returns \f[B]None\f[R] if the event matches learned\-normal behavior.
.PP
\f[B]observe_tokens\f[R] is identical but accepts pre\-computed tokens
(useful when the caller has already tokenized the line).
.PP
\f[B]sweep\f[R] scans all profiles for events/systems that have gone
silent.
It should be called periodically (e.g.\ once per minute).
